# Grid A — S1 Explain / Mechanism enumeration (gate.Run)
#
# Targets: architecture_explain scenario + ReqMechanism + ShapeStepList.
# Question asks for the 9 gate checks in order. Correct answers must
# enumerate the check names; hand-wavy "validates many things" answers
# fail both positive and negative.
#
# Ground truth (internal/analysis/gate/gate.go, as of commit 24+):
# the 9 checks in registration order are:
#
#   - Always (read + write):
#     1. coverage           (gate.go:127)
#     2. dag_closure        (gate.go:128)
#     3. budget_sanity      (gate.go:129)
#
#   - Read-mode only:
#     4. contract_complete       (gate.go:135)
#     5. hypothesis_coverage     (gate.go:136)
#     6. subtopic_coherence      (gate.go:144)  [commit 24+ coherence pair]
#     7. shape_subject_coherence (gate.go:145)  [commit 24+ coherence pair]
#
#   - Always (post):
#     8. criterion_resolvable    (gate.go:147)
#     9. pending_fields_wellformed (gate.go:148; SOFT — only soft check)
#
# Each check has two equally-valid references: the registered
# GateCheck.Name string (snake_case) and the Go function identifier
# (CamelCase, check<Name>). LLM answers routinely pick one or the
# other depending on prose voice; both forms are grounded in gate.go,
# so the gate accepts either via EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX alternation.
# The retry-continuation detail is a subtle follow-up that
# distinguishes a grounded answer from generic prose.
#
# EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS catches contract.Check's sub-functions
# (checkCitations / checkMustInclude / checkMustExclude /
# checkAcceptance, plus a never-defined checkSymbolsSanity that LLMs
# have invented). Note: `checkShape` is INTENTIONALLY OMITTED from
# the blacklist after 2026-05-01 — the gate has its own legitimate
# `checkShapeSubjectCoherence` function, and a substring matcher
# would false-positive on it (s1a-20260501-082338 trace). The 4
# remaining contract.Check sub-function names + checkSymbolsSanity
# still catch the "blended gate.Run with contract.Check" failure
# mode the original docstring described; only `checkShape` had the
# substring conflict.
#
# The 2026-04-22 s1a-115146 run-1 trace showed an answer that
# silently blended gate.Run's checks with contract.Check's checks
# because a sub-topic entity leak anchored Explorer onto
# contract/checker.go. The fix (A': sub-topic entity narrowing + B:
# PendingReads drain) closes the routing hole; this negative gate is
# a tripwire in case the hole reopens.
ID="s1a"
NAME="mechanism enumeration — gate.Run ordered checks"
QUESTION="gate.Run 的 9 项检查是按什么顺序跑的？遇到 retryable reject 时后续检查是否继续执行？"
EXPECT_CONTAINS="gate.Run coverage"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX='(dag_closure|DAGClosure)
(contract_complete|ContractComplete)
(criterion_resolvable|CriterionResolvable)'
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py BaseAgent.java checkSymbolsSanity checkCitations checkMustInclude checkMustExclude checkAcceptance"
